  "summary": "Three November 2026 preprints apply quantum-mechanical frameworks to electrodynamics in time-varying and resonant optical systems.",
  "synthesis": "Three preprints from November 2026 develop quantum-mechanical formalisms for electromagnetic wave propagation and light-matter coupling. Two address time-varying optical media. One presents a semiclassical theory that links frequency-time operators to quantum mechanics. The other models a time-modulated dispersive medium from an ensemble of laser-dressed quantum emitters and solves Maxwell's equations using Floquet theory. The third applies Feshbach projection to derive a Hermitian light-matter Hamiltonian for a mechanical oscillator coupled to a one-dimensional electromagnetic field. The common thread is the use of operator-based quantum formalisms to describe classical field dynamics. The new element is the derivation of effective optical descriptions from explicit microscopic quantum structure.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
